    "explanation": "The cerebellum is located infratentorially within the posterior\ncranial fossa and lies between the temporal and occipital lobes\nof the brainstem.\nThe three primary functions of the cerebellum are:\n• Maintenance of posture and balance\n• Maintenance of muscle tone\n• Coordination of voluntary motor activity",
