    "explanation": "The fibula is the slender lateral bone of the leg that does not\nparticipate in the articulation at the knee joint but does take\npart in the ankle joint below.\nThe knee joint is the largest and most complicated joint in the\nbody. It consists of two main parts:\n(1) paired condylar joints between the rounded medial and\nlateral condyles of the femur above and the corresponding\ncondyles of the tibia and their cartilaginous menisci below, and\n(2) a gliding joint between the patella and the patellar surface\nof the femur.",
