    "explanation": "Centroacinar cells are low cuboidal cells with pale cytoplasm\nthat form the initial segment of the intercalated ducts in the\nexocrine pancreas.\nThey secrete an enzyme-poor alkaline fluid when stimulated\nby secretin.\n(Choice B) Secretin is a hormone produced by S cells in the\nsmall intestine. It stimulates bicarbonate secretion by the\npancreas and biliary tract.\n(Choice C) Glucagon is produced in the endocrine pancreas\n(islets of Langerhans)\n(Choice D) Pancreatic digestive enzymes are synthesized\nby the acinar cells of the exocrine pancreas.",
