    "explanation": "The hypothalamus forms the lower part of the lateral\nwall (ventral walls) and the floor of the third ventricle.\nThe ventricles of the brain consist of:\n• Two lateral ventricles\n• Third ventricle\n• Fourth ventricle\nCommunication pathways within the ventricles of the brain are\nsummarized below:\n• Lateral ventricles → third ventricle\nvia interventricular foramina of Monro\n• Third ventricle → fourth ventricle via cerebral\naqueduct of Sylvius\n• Fourth ventricle → subarachnoid space via the\no Foramina of Luschka= lateral\no Foramen of Magendie= medial",
