    "explanation": "Hirschsprung disease is caused by failed migration of neural\ncrest cells, leading to absence of the Auerbach and\nMeissner plexuses in the distal colon. This presents with:\n• Bilious emesis\n• Failure to pass meconium in the first 48 hours and\nchronic constipation\n• Dilation of the proximal, unaffected colon, resulting in\na transition zone\n• Explosive expulsion of feces (squirt sign) but empty\nrectum on digital exam\nDiagnosis: Rectal suction biopsy showing absence of\nganglion cells\nTreatment: Resection",
