    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "The ejaculatory ducts are formed by the union of the\nductus deferens with the ducts of the seminal vesicle.\nThe ejaculatory ducts pierce the posterior surface of the\nprostate and open into the prostatic part of the urethra, near\nthe margin of the prostatic utricle. The function of the\nejaculatory ducts is to drain the seminal fluid into the\nprostatic urethra.\n(Choice C) The epididymis functions in the maturation and\nstorage of spermatozoa. It connects the efferent ductules of\nthe testis to the ductus deferens.\n(Choice D) The bulbourethral glands lie beneath the\nsphincter urethrae muscle and enter the penile urethra.",
