    "explanation": "The lumbar cistern is an enlarged subarachnoid space\naround the cauda equina that spans from vertebral levels L1\nto S2.\nLumbar taps or spinal taps are done in the subarachnoid\nspace in the region of the lumbar cistern (usually between\nthe laminae of L3 and L4 or L4 and L5)",
