    "explanation": "The short muscles of the thumb are the following:\n• Opponens pollicis\n• Abductor pollicis brevis\n• Flexor pollicis brevis\n• Adductor pollicis\nThe first three of these muscles form the thenar eminence.\nOn the other hand, the following muscles make up\nthe hypothenar eminence:\n• Opponens digiti minimi\n• Abductor digiti minimi\n• Flexor digiti minimi brevis\nRemember: OAF\nBoth groups of muscles perform the same function:\nOppose, Abduct, and Flex!",
