    "explanation": "The bronchial arteries, which supply oxygenated blood to the\nnonrespiratory conducting tissues of the lungs, arise from the\ndescending aorta.\nBronchial Arteries\n• Originate from the thoracic aorta\n• Typically, one artery serves the right lung, while two\narteries serve the left lung\n• Provide oxygenated blood to the nonrespiratory\nconducting tissues of the lungs and the visceral\npleura\n• Anastomoses take place between the capillaries of the\nbronchial and pulmonary systems",
