    "id": "superexam-anatomy-0101",
    "subject": "anatomy",
    "originalNumber": 101,
    "stem": "A 30 y/o female patient is brought to the emergency room in\nrespiratory distress. On PE she has an anterior neck mass,\nwhich relatives recounted that it recently suddenly increased\nin size. You decided to create an emergency airway to retore\nrespiration. At what level could you rapidly create an airway\nwith minimum danger of hemorrhage and damage to the\nvocal cords?",
