    "explanation": "the lateral cord give rise to lateral pectoral nerve (\npectoralis major), musculocutaneous nerve (\ncoracobrachialis, biceps brachii, brachialis,\nsensory to the lateral border of the foreeam) and\nlateral root of the median nerve. A- is supplied by\nthe radial nerve which is a branch of the posterior\ncord. C and D- pt will only have weakness but not\ninability since the supinator muscle is supplied by\nthe radial nerve eventhough the biceps brachii is\ndenervated. on the otherhand, there is still some\nflexion of the forearm because of the reverse\naction of other forearm muscle as well as the\npartial innervation of brachialis by the radial\nnerve. ( Snell 9th ed Regions p 354)",
