    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Inside each cavernous sinus is the internal carotid\nartery with its small branches, surrounded by the\ncarotid plexus of sympathetic nerve(s), and the\nabducent nerve. The oculomotor (CN III) and\ntrochlear (CN IV) nerves, plus two of the three\ndivisions of the trigeminal nerve (CN V1 and V2)\nare embedded in the lateral wall of the sinus.\nMoore 7th pg 869",
