    "explanation": "The utricle and saccule constitute the static\nlabyrinth which functions during the linear\nacceleration of the head and with the effects of the\npull of gravity. On the other hand, the semicircular\ncanals make up the kinetic labyrinth which is\nimportant in angular deceleration and\nacceleration; it has no otoliths.",
