    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Contraction of the orbicularis oculi muscle is\nprimarily responsible for the clinically observed\nperiorbital crow's feet. The orbicularis oculi\nmuscle is bordered superolaterally by fibers of the\nfrontalis muscle and medially by the levator\npalpebrae muscle. The frontalis muscle and the\ncorrugator muscle are responsible for the\nappearance of wrinkles and vertical frown lines\naccordingly. The procerus muscle, which overlies\nthe nasal root, is responsible for a snout-nose\nappearance and horizontal frown lines.",
