    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "The 3rd branchial arch gives rise to the greater\nhorn of the hyoid, stylopharyngeus muscle and CN\nIX. Therefore, if it fails to form or mature to adult\nstructures, patient would be expected to present\nwith deficiency of the greater horn of the hyoid\nand lack of stylopharynegus muscle. And since CN\nIX would be absent, there would be also be poor\ngag reflex and decreased parotid gland secretion.",
