    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "Varicocole is the engorgement of the venous\ndrainage of the testis, the pampiniform plexus. It\nusually presents with enlargement of the scrotum\nand examination would reveal \"bag of worms\"\nappearance. Varicocoel is more commonly\nobserved in the left scrotum, which drains to the\nleft renal vein and is subjected to higher pressure\nthan the right. Hence, varicocoele is usually\nassociated with renal tumors or other pathologies\nthat may increase renal vein pressure.",
