    "explanation": "The common peroneal nerve is the root of\nsuperficial and deep peroneal nerve. If it was\naffected, signs of deep peroneal nerve lesion must\nalso be present (like weak or no dorsiflexion). The\nsuperficial peroneal nerve is responsible for\neversion and plantar flexion. Tibial nerve is for\nplantar flexion only. Common fibular nerve is the\nother term for common peroneal nerve.",
